NAME
    err - an error message on the console (#include "../lib_err.c")

SYNOPSIS
    #include "../lib_err.c"
    eputs("cmd: not found");

DESCRIPTION
    eputs(s) prints s and a line feed on the console. Today that is
    what puts() does: Y1/OS has no output redirection, so the output IS
    the console. It stays a function of its own so that when the shell
    gets > and pipes, every command's diagnostics move to the raw
    console in one place, as the P8X eputs does: a "not found" must
    never land in an output file or a pipe.

    Convention: eputs for failures, including a usage message printed
    because the arguments were wrong; puts for output, including the
    usage asked for with -h.

NOTES
    Changed from the P8X version: putchar instead of the PUTS and
    CONOUT BIOS calls.
    Ported from P8X os/commands/lib_err.c 2026-09-23.

